  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate action and solar energy development programme in the Tarapac&#xe1; Region in Chile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The international financing mechanism leaded by the GCF and CAF will support a project (Atacama Solar), expanding the photovoltaic solar energy projects scale in an area where the electricity generation matrix is highly intensive in thermoelectricity (intensive in GHG emissions), making it more competitive in 
one of the main mining development regions in Chile.

&#x2022; It helps Chile to displace fossil fuel capacity, increase resilience to climate change, and reduce emissions, by using renewables instead of fossil fuels.
&#x2022; It is a scalable project which plans to expand by 107 MW upon completion of the current project.
&#x2022; It would serve as a demonstrative project for other hydro-dependant nations in the Latin American and African regions, which are also experiencing similar effects of climate change on declining hydrology, as a result of which they need to resort to fossil fuels.</narrative>
  </description>
